        "Now when Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, the son of Saul, was come to David, he fell on his face, and did reverence. And David said, “Mephibosheth.” And he answered, “Behold your servant!”",
        "And David said to him, “Fear not: for I will surely show you kindness for Jonathan your father’s sake, and will restore you all the land of Saul your father; and you will eat bread at my table continually.”",
        "And he bowed himself, and said, “What is your servant, that you should look upon such a dead dog as I am?”",
